# Dev tooling follow-up

- Make `cli/commands/thread/send.ts` follow a reply across assistant/compaction
  splits instead of stopping on the first `turn.finished`. Today it exits 0 with
  `status: complete, finalText: null` for an empty first turn even when its
  successor later fails with `context_window_exceeded`. Follow the execution's
  successor selector through completion; apply the same semantics to
  `thread/tail.ts --until-idle`. Reproduce by scripting mock overflow, summary,
  overflow and comparing `thread send` with the final snapshot and journal.
  Until fixed, assert split outcomes from snapshots and journal events, not the
  send command's early terminal envelope.

- Align `cli/commands/thread/transcript.ts` generic custom-block output with
  `docs/debugging.md`'s untruncated JSON contract. `thread view --json` still
  clips an unknown custom block's `summary` unless `--full` is also passed.
  The dedicated `thread-reference` projection exposes all props, but handoff
  cards still need `--full` for complete frozen text. Reproduce with a handoff
  seed and compare `thread view --json` against `thread view --full --json`.

- Let `./mf doc read|put` and `./mf thread send --ref` name a chat lineage's
  Scratch note (`scratch://@c12/x`). They send no `rootThreadId`, so a lineage
  note is reachable only through `./mf api ... rootThreadId=<first chat id>`.
  Fix in `cli/commands/doc/` and the thread send reference path when a probe
  needs it.

- Give the dev log directory and Nitro's watcher exclusion one source of truth.
  `apps/server/nitro.config.ts` builds its own `<repo>/logs/**` exclusion while
  `lib/dev-env.ts` `resolveDevLogDir` resolves `LOG_DIR` (honoring any absolute
  override); moving one without the other lets JSONL mirror writes rebuild Nitro
  and orphan in-flight replies. Export one typed dev-runtime path both consume.

- Make `db:generate` derive its next numeric filename ordinal from the highest
  existing tag, not Drizzle's journal idx. The frozen idx/tag offset makes default
  generation overwrite older snapshots (0071 and 0072 were overwritten after
  tag 0076). Until automated, follow the timestamp-prefix workflow in
  `packages/database/.context/CONTEXT.md`; never rewrite applied identities.

- Make the orphan sweep (`lib/worktree-cleanup-orphans.ts`) tolerate dead panes.
  Under `set -g remain-on-exit on` (the owner's `~/.tmux.conf` has it) a pane
  whose process exited stays listed with an empty `pane_current_path`, and
  `listPanes` throws "Could not inspect tmux pane ownership". Any dead pane on
  `meridian-dev` then fails the sweep at the start of `pnpm dev`, and a SIGTERM
  during an orphan stop fails its own ownership recheck. Read `#{pane_dead}`;
  skip a dead pane's cwd check and keep its PID out of the signal roots (the PID
  may be reused); let a session with only dead panes still be reaped when its
  name, path and checkout prove ownership. The orphan tests pass `-f /dev/null`
  so this config does not leak in.
